How DbContext is registered (implementation details)
•	Infrastructure exposes an extension method:
•	IServiceCollection AddNovaBankingInfrastructure(this IServiceCollection services, IConfiguration configuration)
•	That method reads the connection string from configuration via configuration.GetConnectionString("NovaBanking").
•	If a non-empty connection string exists, the method calls services.AddDbContext<NovaBankingDbContext>(options => options.UseSqlServer(connectionString));
•	NovaBanking.Api calls builder.Services.AddNovaBankingInfrastructure(builder.Configuration) during startup (Program.cs).
How configuration is loaded
•	Connection string is read from standard ASP.NET Core configuration:
•	Configuration key: ConnectionStrings:NovaBanking
•	The connection string is expected to be provided via user secrets / environment variables / other configuration providers you have configured locally. No secrets were added to source code.
Safe database connectivity check
•	/health endpoint (Api) behavior:
•	Creates a scope, requests NovaBankingDbContext from DI.
•	If DbContext is not registered (no connection string), returns status = "Healthy", database = "NotConfigured".
•	If DbContext is present, runs await db.Database.CanConnectAsync() and returns:
•	200 OK { status = "Healthy", database = "Connected" } if true
•	503 (Service Unavailable) if false or on exception
•	Exceptions are caught and not exposed; no sensitive details are returned.
